# Bilingual site synchronization

- Japanese pages under `site/` and English mirrors under `site/en/` are one feature.
- When changing visible copy, navigation, links, forms, metadata, dynamic UI text, or infographics, update both languages in the same change.
- Preserve page pairs and query parameters when switching languages, especially `slug`, `q`, and `s`.
- Keep external source headlines in their original language when no verified translation exists; explain this in English UI instead of inventing a translation.
- Run `python scripts/check_bilingual.py` after changes.
- Run `python scripts/check_bilingual.py --update-manifest` only after reviewing both language versions.
- Do not commit if the bilingual check fails.
